    #points([The test-only JOSE 1.11.13 oracle includes upstream security and OTP 29 fixes. Root and consumer builds run `gleam build --warnings-as-errors`, and authored Erlang compiles with `erlc -Werror`. No deprecated-catch compiler exception is required. #adr(22) supersedes the exception in #adr(16).], [Mandatory CI runs the canonical local gate on pull requests and pushes to `main`, and its final status rejects failed, cancelled or skipped mandatory jobs. CI builds Sinal, HTTP Gun, Relay and JSON Blueprint from Hex at the versions and checksums locked in each `manifest.toml`, with read-only repository permissions and no persisted credentials. #adr(15) #adr(20)], [CI caches Hex archives and path-dependency fingerprints but no compiled output. Dependency preparation retries explicit Hex rate limits at most three times. Compiler and test failures are never retried.], [OpenID verdicts default to strict, so every selected module finishes PASSED. Regression mode permits only the exact SKIPPED unsigned-token and REVIEW logout outcomes in `test/conformance/known-outcomes.json`, which remain non-pass evidence. Third-party interruption, unknown outcomes, driver errors, missing modules, malformed evidence and empty selections fail both policies. Neither policy confers certification.], [The conformance driver archives a terminal or unready setup status and its module log before starting the reference relying party. The driver is used by the optional provider-conformance workflow.], [Each workflow retains bounded artifacts with package and sibling revisions and logs, and provider jobs retain image and browser identities. Artifacts exclude generated PKI and private keys, and a run never overwrites checked-in raw history.], [Nix pins all tooling through `flake.lock`. The formatter excludes frozen evidence receipts, deliberate negative compiler fixtures and generated output.], [Repository documentation consists of the design layer, the README files, `AGENTS.md`, the compiled usage examples, #lnk("../ORACLE.md")[the oracle references] and #lnk("../BENCHMARKS.md")[the benchmark measurements]. #adr(10)])
  ]
