    #points([`gleam.toml` owns admitted dependency ranges, and `manifest.toml` records one concrete resolution that does not qualify every admitted version. Runtime and test-only dependencies stay separate: oidcc, erlang-jose and telemetry_registry are development oracles that an application does not install by using Hellhound.], [A release records the actual package, sibling, dependency, fixture and toolchain revisions and replaces unpublished sibling Git dependencies with approved release declarations. It reviews resolved upstream changelogs, licenses and advisories, produces the release SBOM, and checks advisory-query coverage against known controls. An empty query result never establishes absence of vulnerabilities.], [A changed dependency or fixture pin runs the relevant provider, conformance and compatibility suites. Failed, skipped and human-review results stay distinct from passed assertions, and an older receipt never qualifies a new resolution or pin. #adr(8)])
  ]
  #subsection(title: "Benchmark method")[
    #points([The retained benchmark entry points are `hellhound_fetch_ownership_test:benchmark/0` and `snapshot_benchmark/0`, run from `gleam shell` with four schedulers. Each starts its own local HTTPS test provider and stops each client fixture. `benchmark/0` warms 100 validations per client, measures 3 000 per client for one and four clients and 3 000 per caller for four concurrent callers of one client, reports throughput and latency percentiles, and measures 100 sequential unknown-key refresh requests after an untimed setup fetch, so within the cooldown they return the cached snapshot without fetching. `snapshot_benchmark/0` warms 1 000 reads per cache and measures 20 000 per cache for one and four caches.], [Benchmark output is an observation of one checkout on one machine, never a deployment capacity guarantee or a correctness-gate threshold. A reported result retains its raw output, source and dependency revisions and machine configuration. The retained measurements are in #lnk("../BENCHMARKS.md")[BENCHMARKS.md], which links to the oracle references. #adr(17)])
  ]
